			],
			"Message": "style(Common): Normalize README list separators from em dash to hyphen\n\nReplace all Unicode em dash (`—`) characters with ASCII hyphens (`-`) used as description separators in markdown bullet points, numbered lists, bold feature headings, and table cell prose across the Overview, Key Features, Security, Compatibility, and Related Documentation sections. Also collapse a two-line hanging indent on the final `CHANGELOG.md` list item to a single continuation line.\n\nThis eliminates mixed Unicode/ASCII dash conventions in the README, converging on plain ASCII hyphens for list-inline descriptions while em dashes are preserved only in natural-language prose contexts outside list structures.",
			"SHA": "440e58a1e9e24cda8cc6f4336a9c8efe2d5501ce"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
